# End-of-line contract. This is a tooling invariant, not a style preference:
# removing it breaks digests and makes `git status` unreliable.
#
# Under `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) a text file is checked
# out as CRLF while its blob stays LF. The index caches the CRLF file's stat size.
# When any tool then rewrites that file in LF, the size no longer matches and
# git's `ie_modified` fast path returns DATA_CHANGED WITHOUT comparing content:
# `git status` reports the path as modified while `git diff` and
# `git diff --cached` are both empty and `git hash-object` equals the index blob.
# Pinning `eol=lf` makes the checkout itself LF, so what tools write is what git
# expects and the phantom mark cannot appear.
#
# It also makes byte-level identity platform-independent. `computeEvaluatorDigest`
# and `computeInferenceCoreDigest` hash the bytes ON DISK, and `git archive`
# applies the `eol` attribute; with the attribute unset, the same commit yields a
# different digest on a CRLF checkout than on an LF one.
#
# Measuring CRLF in Git Bash: `grep -c $'\r'` matches EVERY line, because grep
# strips the CR in text mode. Use `od -c`, or count bytes in Python.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats present in this repository's tree. `text=auto` already applies
# git's own NUL-byte heuristic, so an unlisted binary is normally detected and
# left alone; these marks pin the cases where that heuristic is the only defence,
# because a binary run through EOL conversion is silent file corruption. Every
# extension below was found on disk under this worktree — all are gitignored
# today, which is exactly why the marks matter: they must already be in force the
# first time one is staged.

# Model and inference assets: public/models/**/onnx, public/vendor/transformers-wasm,
# benchmark/data/checkpoints/**.
*.onnx binary
*.wasm binary
*.safetensors binary

# Archives. benchmark/data/*.tgz exist here; the four source snapshots are .bz2
# and .zip, and the external Madras set is .parquet.
*.7z binary
*.bz2 binary
*.gz binary
*.parquet binary
*.tgz binary
*.xz binary
*.zip binary

# Python bench by-products: __pycache__ under benchmark/lab, pickled estimators.
*.pkl binary
*.pyc binary

# The pinned Chrome for Testing build under .cache/. Never committed, but a
# `git add -f` of that tree must not mangle it.
*.bin binary
*.dat binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.hyb binary
*.pak binary
*.pb binary

# NOT binary despite the name: benchmark/data/candidates/**/*.raw are raw JSON
# provider responses, and *.jsonl is the corpus line format. Both are text and
# must normalize to LF like everything else.
